WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.760
Picture the only gas station on a long,

2
00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:04.720
empty desert highway.

3
00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:07.790
Drivers running low have
no close substitute.

4
00:00:07.790 --> 00:00:10.360
There is nowhere else to fill up.

5
00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:15.390
In economics, a single seller with
no close substitutes is a monopoly.

6
00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:17.630
So why doesn't the owner
just charge the highest

7
00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:20.040
price anyone could ever pay?

8
00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:23.020
In this mission, you'll build
the monopoly graph and find

9
00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:25.810
the quantity and price a monopolist picks.

10
00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:28.280
Then you'll drag output in a graph lab,

11
00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:30.140
predict the most profitable point,

12
00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:31.310
and test it.

13
00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:35.550
Your mission: find out how a
monopolist really chooses its price.
